  "conclusions": [
    "Hard routing alone did not improve complete-task success on the tested reset, but Panda no-ACT held the ball for77ticks and achieved59held-lift ticks before failing transport.",
    "The boundary objective improved validation transition-pair accuracy from25/28 to27/28 while losing the held-lift outcome in the matched Panda rollout.",
    "Open/closed jaw predictions can still contradict the reported component phase on out-of-distribution states; hard routing alone supplies no semantic jaw constraint.",
    "History augmentation has no closed-loop evidence in this experiment; its held-out action errors were slightly worse than hard-only heads.",
    "Actual learner-visited correction data and achieved/issued history are needed; offline phase accuracy is insufficient to select task-successful policies.",
    "The explicitly assisted phase guard did not improve the tested Panda reset; its held/lift counts are reported separately from learned-only outcomes."
  ],
